msgid "Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:42
msgid ""
"Error, warning, and help messages now state what pipx found and what to run "
"next, without hedges such as \"already seems to be installed\" or "
"\"Perhaps\". Update scripts that match the old message text (:pr:`2376`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:51
msgid ""
"A pipx that changed its own environment, through ``pipx upgrade pipx`` or "
"``pipx reinstall pipx`` for example, no longer crashes with an "
"``ImportError`` when another pipx command empties the trash while it is "
"still running, such as during the rest of ``pipx upgrade-all``. The copy of "
"its environment it imports from now stays in the trash until the process "
"exits (:pr:`2397`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:55
msgid ""
"Interrupting a parallel ``pipx reinstall-all`` with Ctrl-C now gives a "
"restored environment back the shared app, man page or completion links "
"another environment took while the rebuild had it in the trash, as a failed "
"rebuild already did (:pr:`2386`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:58
msgid ""
"On Windows under the uv backend, ``pipx run --refresh`` or ``--no-cache`` of "
"a local script no longer deletes the cached environment while another run of "
"the same script is still executing in it, and neither does the expiry sweep. "
"Such a run builds a throwaway environment for itself instead, and after ``--"
"refresh`` the next run to find the cached one idle rebuilds it (:pr:`2387`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:62
msgid ""
"On Windows under the uv backend, ``pipx upgrade pipx`` on a pipx that "
"manages itself no longer fails with ``Access is denied`` and rolls back. uv "
"deletes the files it replaces, which Windows refuses for the running "
"``pipx.exe``, so pipx now moves that launcher to its trash first, where the "
"next pipx command deletes it (:pr:`2396`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:66
msgid ""
"Where pipx copies launchers instead of linking them, as on Windows without "
"symlink rights, ``pipx reinstall`` and ``pipx install --force`` no longer "
"warn ``Overwriting file`` for the package's own launcher. Windows ``.exe`` "
"launchers embed their build time, so a rebuilt one never matched its old "
"copy byte for byte and every reinstall warned. pipx now recognises its own "
"copy by the interpreter it names and replaces it without a warning; a file "
"another venv or the user put there still gets one (:pr:`2394`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:71
msgid ""
"With the uv backend and ``UV_LINK_MODE=symlink``, ``pipx uninstall`` now "
"removes the man page and shell completion links it exposed, and ``pipx "
"list`` no longer reports those man pages as missing. uv makes the "
"environment's own copies symlinks into its cache, and pipx followed them "
"there instead of stopping at the environment (:pr:`2380`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:75
msgid ""
"``--fetch-python`` and ``pipx interpreter upgrade`` now download and unpack "
"the standalone Python build next to the interpreter directory instead of in "
"the system temp dir, so a tmpfs ``/tmp`` or a ``/tmp`` on another btrfs "
"subvolume no longer forces a full copy of the build into the pipx home or "
"splits its hard links into separate files (:pr:`2403`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:79
msgid ""
"``pipx inject pipx`` without ``--include-apps`` and ``pipx runpip pipx`` on "
"a pipx that manages itself no longer mix old and new pipx code when they "
"change the pipx package. Like ``pipx upgrade pipx``, they now load late "
"imports from a copy of the environment, which the next pipx command deletes "
"from the trash (:pr:`2393`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:82
msgid ""
"``pipx list --json`` no longer exports the interpreter a self-managed pipx "
"recorded when that path no longer leads to the interpreter its environment "
"runs on, such as a removed bootstrap environment's ``python3``. ``pipx "
"install-all`` then builds that environment on the default interpreter "
"instead of whatever appears at the old path (:pr:`2389`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:86
msgid ""
"``pipx reinstall pipx`` on a pipx that manages itself no longer crashes with "
"an ``ImportError`` when it installs a different pipx version. Modules the "
"running pipx imported late came from the version it was installing, so old "
"and new code mixed. It now loads them from its own moved environment, which "
"the next pipx command deletes from the trash (:pr:`2377`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:90
msgid ""
"``pipx upgrade pipx``, ``pipx upgrade-all`` and ``pipx install --force "
"pipx`` on a pipx that manages itself no longer crash with an ``ImportError`` "
"when they install a different pipx version. The running pipx now loads its "
"late imports from a copy of its environment, which the next pipx command "
"deletes from the trash (:pr:`2388`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:94
msgid ""
"pipx now recognises the app copies it made when the environment's "
"interpreter path is too long for a shebang line or contains a space. pip and "
"uv start such launchers with a ``#!/bin/sh`` line that hands over to the "
"interpreter, and pipx took ``/bin/sh`` for the interpreter, so ``pipx "
"reinstall`` kept a stale copy and warned \"File exists ... Not modifying.\" "
"(:pr:`2392`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:102 ../../../changelog.rst:461
#: ../../../changelog.rst:533
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:104
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` now names its cached environments with an HMAC keyed by a "
"random per-user secret, stored with mode ``0600`` in ``.run-key`` inside the "
"run cache. Before, the name was a plain hash of inputs that include tokens "
"and proxy passwords from the environment, so another account that could list "
"the cache could check guesses at those values against it. Existing cache "
"entries are not reused and expire as usual (:pr:`2370`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:108
msgid ""
"pipx no longer records an abbreviation of a one-shot pip option that the "
"current pip finds ambiguous but an older pip accepts, such as ``--requirem "
"FILE``, which pip 24.0 reads as ``--requirement FILE``. With such a shared "
"pip, a later ``pipx upgrade`` or ``pipx reinstall`` used to replay it and "
"install from whatever another account had put at that path. An existing "
"record drops it when read, and an abbreviation that could name a source "
"option such as ``--constraint`` goes through the same replay check as that "
"option (:pr:`2390`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:113
msgid ""
"pipx no longer records an interpreter that lives inside another virtual "
"environment, such as the ``python3`` of an activated bootstrap environment "
"or of one made with ``python3 -m venv --copies``. It records the base "
"interpreter named in that environment's ``pyvenv.cfg``, which outlives the "
"bootstrap. ``pipx install-all`` also stops building on an exported "
"interpreter that sits inside a virtual environment or that another account "
"can change, and uses the default Python with a message instead, so a "
"snapshot taken before the bootstrap was removed no longer runs whatever "
"another account later puts at its old path (:pr:`2402`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:123
msgid "`1.18.9 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.18.9>`_ - 2026-10-29"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:130
msgid ""
"Extend the 1.18.8 handling of recorded pip arguments to uv's path options "
"and to ``--group``. pipx no longer records ``--group``, which names a "
"``pyproject.toml`` to read packages from, like ``-r``. On POSIX, a recorded "
"``--config-file``, ``--project``, ``--directory``, ``--overrides``/``--"
"override`` or ``--excludes``/``--exclude`` that points at a path another "
"account could change stops ``pipx upgrade``, ``pipx reinstall`` and the "
"other replaying commands with the same error as ``--find-links``. ``pipx "
"list --outdated`` runs the same check and reports such an environment as "
"failed instead of querying the recorded location. ``pipx runpip`` reads its "
"install arguments with the same parser, so it records an install written as "
"``-qe ./project`` or ``-e./project`` as editable (:pr:`2363`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:138
msgid ""
"When a rebuild fails during a parallel ``pipx reinstall-all``, the restored "
"environment gets back the shared app, man page or completion links another "
"environment took while the rebuild had it in the trash, unless something "
"outside this run has replaced them since (:pr:`2371`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:141
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` no longer reuses a cached environment after a change to a "
"variable outside ``PIP_*`` and ``UV_*`` that decides which config file pip "
"or uv reads, which proxy or index answers, which certificate is trusted or "
"which credentials are sent, such as ``XDG_CONFIG_HOME``, ``SSL_CERT_FILE``, "
"``HTTPS_PROXY`` or ``NETRC``. The values only feed the cache key's hash, so "
"secrets in them stay out of cache paths and logs (:pr:`2364`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:149
msgid "`1.18.8 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.18.8>`_ - 2026-10-29"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:156
msgid ""
"A ``pipx run`` that names an app the package does not provide, such as "
"``pipx run --spec black blackk``, no longer expires the cached environment, "
"so the corrected command reuses it instead of rebuilding. A failed venv "
"creation or install still expires the entry (:pr:`2354`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:159
msgid ""
"A second Ctrl-C during ``pipx reinstall-all``, ``upgrade-all`` or ``install-"
"all`` no longer hangs pipx. A signal handled just after a worker took the "
"shared lock could leave it held, so every other task waited forever "
"(:pr:`2348`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:162
msgid ""
"A self-managed pipx no longer adopts a recorded default interpreter that no "
"longer backs its own environment, such as the ``python3`` of a bootstrap "
"environment removed after ``pipx install pipx --python python3``. pipx "
"failed every command with a ``PIPX_DEFAULT_PYTHON`` error, or built new "
"environments on whatever appeared at that path later (:pr:`2245`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:166
msgid ""
"Apply ``--cooldown`` and ``PIPX_COOLDOWN`` to the shared pip that the pip "
"backend installs or refreshes during the command. pipx used to fetch the "
"newest pip, even one uploaded minutes earlier, while it held back the "
"package itself. A new shared environment now starts from the oldest pip pipx "
"supports and upgrades only to a release older than the cooldown (:pr:`2311`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:170
msgid ""
"Finish restoring an environment when Ctrl-C, ``SIGTERM`` or ``SIGHUP`` "
"arrives while a failed or interrupted ``pipx reinstall``, ``install --"
"force``, ``inject``, ``upgrade`` or ``manifest sync`` rolls it back. The "
"rollback deletes the half-built environment and then moves the backup in, "
"and a signal between the two steps left the environment deleted and its only "
"copy in the trash, which the next pipx command emptied. pipx now holds such "
"a signal until the backup is back in place and acts on it afterwards "
"(:pr:`2329`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:175
msgid ""
"For an editable install, pipx now copies only the man pages that resolve "
"inside the project directory. Before, it followed absolute paths, ``..`` and "
"symlinks, and a wheel installed by name could ship its own editable "
"``direct_url.json`` to make pipx copy any readable file into the environment "
"and link it as a man page (:pr:`2268`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:179
msgid ""
"Ignore apps, man pages and completions whose name is not a plain file name, "
"such as ``..``, and never delete a directory to make room for an app link, "
"so ``pipx reinstall`` can no longer remove the parent of ``PIPX_BIN_DIR`` "
"(:pr:`2228`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:182
msgid ""
"Ignore recorded ``venv_args`` other than ``--system-site-packages``, with a "
"warning, when reading a snapshot or ``pipx_metadata.json``, so ``pipx "
"install-all`` and ``pipx reinstall`` no longer pass an edited ``--clear "
"<dir>`` or an extra directory to ``python -m venv`` (:pr:`2239`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:185
msgid ""
"Installing an editable project whose man page or project directory is a "
"looping symlink no longer crashes pipx on Python 3.11 and 3.12; pipx skips "
"that man page (:pr:`2334`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:187
msgid ""
"Keep ``pipx reinstall-all``, ``upgrade-all``, and ``install-all`` waiting "
"for the environments they change when pipx can no longer write their output, "
"as with ``pipx reinstall-all 2>&1 | head`` or a closed stderr. pipx used to "
"log a traceback and return while it still rebuilt environments in the "
"background, so an interrupt then skipped the rollback, and an environment "
"waiting for its turn hung (:pr:`2290`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:191
msgid ""
"Keep a command, man page or completion link that another package took over "
"while ``pipx reinstall``, ``reinstall-all``, ``uninject`` or ``uninstall-"
"all`` was running. These commands gathered the environment's links first and "
"deleted them by name later, so a name another package claimed in between, "
"for example in the same parallel ``reinstall-all``, disappeared without a "
"message. pipx now deletes a link only if it still points into the "
"environment by Bernát Gábor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:196
msgid ""
"Keep pipx's ``pipx_metadata.json`` when the installer replaces it with a "
"wheel's data file of the same name. A failed ``pipx install --force``, "
"``pipx upgrade`` or ``pipx inject``, or a ``pipx runpip APP install`` of a "
"dependency, used to leave the wheel's copy in place, and later commands read "
"its index arguments, spec and suffix as pipx's own. pipx now puts its record "
"back after every installer run (:pr:`2269`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:200
msgid ""
"Keep standalone Python archive members inside the unpack directory on Python "
"3.11.0 to 3.11.3, which lack ``tarfile.data_filter``. pipx's own extractor "
"checked member names as text, so a member whose path went through a symlink "
"unpacked earlier from the same archive was written wherever that link led. "
"It now resolves each path through the links already on disk, extracts under "
"normalized names like the data filter does, and refuses a hard link to a "
"symlink (:pr:`2279`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:205
msgid ""
"Keep the apps, manual pages, and completions of injected packages exposed "
"when ``pipx manifest sync`` reinstalls an existing environment, and expose "
"the environment again when the sync is interrupted. pipx used to drop those "
"links without a message, so another package could take the freed names "
"without ``--force``, and an interrupted sync left the rolled-back "
"environment unexposed (:pr:`2273`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:209
msgid ""
"Keep the environment when ``pipx install --force`` or ``pipx install-all --"
"force`` cannot move it aside before a ``Requires-Python`` rebuild. On "
"Windows the move fails while any file inside the environment is open, and "
"pipx then deleted the environment and reported a ``FileNotFoundError`` "
"instead of the real error. pipx now retries the move the way ``pipx "
"reinstall`` does, and if it still fails it leaves the environment in place "
"and reports the original error (:pr:`2350`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:214
msgid ""
"Keep the recorded source of a local wheel when ``pipx runpip <venv> "
"install`` abbreviates a value-taking pip option whose value names the "
"package, such as ``--only-bin <name>`` for ``--only-binary <name>``, and "
"record an install through an abbreviated ``--editable``, such as ``--edit "
"<path>``, as editable (:pr:`2225`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:217
msgid ""
"Keep the rollback backup of a running ``pipx reinstall``, ``reinstall-all``, "
"``install --force``, ``upgrade`` or ``inject`` when another pipx command "
"starts. Every command used to empty the trash at startup, so a ``pipx list`` "
"run meanwhile deleted the backup, and when the first command then failed or "
"was interrupted it lost the environment with a ``FileNotFoundError``. pipx "
"now skips a backup while its environment's lock is held and removes it only "
"once orphaned (:pr:`2298`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:222
msgid ""
"Leave a command, man page or completion that the environment did not expose "
"before with its owner when ``pipx reinstall``, ``reinstall-all``, "
"``interpreter upgrade``, the repair step of ``pipx upgrade``, or a repeated "
"``pipx manifest sync`` rebuilds the environment. These used to replace such "
"a file as if ``--force`` had been passed, deleting a user's own script or "
"repointing another environment's command, although ``pipx install`` had left "
"it alone with a warning. A name two environments both declare now stays with "
"the one that held it, instead of going to whichever ``reinstall-all`` "
"rebuilt last (:pr:`2321`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:228
msgid ""
"Leave an existing environment alone in ``pipx install-all`` without ``--"
"force``. pipx said it was not modifying the environment, then injected the "
"snapshot's ``injected_packages`` into it anyway. Pass ``--force`` to bring "
"existing environments in line with the snapshot (:pr:`2333`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:231
msgid ""
"Let an environment take over an app, manual page, or completion name whose "
"link points to a file that another installed environment no longer ships. "
"pipx before 1.18.0 left such links behind when an upgrade dropped an app, "
"and pipx kept them as collisions that only ``--force`` cleared. A link "
"counts as left over when the environment it points into no longer lists the "
"file in its metadata. The collision warning for a link whose target is "
"missing now says so (:pr:`2356`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:236
msgid ""
"Mask URL passwords and tokens in the remaining places that printed or logged "
"them as typed: the ``Injecting packages`` log line, the ``--output json`` "
"error fields of ``inject``, ``install`` and ``uninject``, the progress lines "
"of ``pipx run`` script dependencies and ``--preinstall``, the local source "
"that ``pipx upgrade`` reports, invalid requirement errors from manifests and "
"inline script metadata, ``--pip-args`` rejected by the uv backend of ``pipx "
"run``, the \"looks like a path\" error, and installer output that pipx "
"captures and logs (:pr:`2252`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:241
msgid ""
"Mask a URL password that contains a literal space or tab, such as ``--index-"
"url \"http://alice:correct horse@host/simple\"``, in the command log, ``--"
"verbose`` output and messages; pipx now masks each argument of a command "
"line before joining it (:pr:`2241`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:244
msgid ""
"Mask the user part of URL credentials that contain a colon, so a token "
"written as ``https://TOKEN:@host`` or ``TOKEN:x-oauth-basic@`` no longer "
"shows in the command log, ``--verbose`` output and messages. Such URLs now "
"show as ``****:****@``, which also hides a plain user name such as ``alice`` "
"(:pr:`2244`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:247
msgid ""
"On Windows under the uv backend, ``pipx run script.py`` now releases the run-"
"cache lock before the script starts. pipx held it until the script exited, "
"so a second run of the same script waited without a message, and a script "
"that ran itself through pipx never finished (:pr:`2352`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:250
msgid ""
"Refuse ``pipx install --lock`` and ``pipx manifest sync`` with a lock under "
"the pip backend when the environment's pip is older than 26.1. That pip read "
"``pylock.toml`` as a requirements file: a real lock failed with a confusing "
"``Invalid requirement`` error, and a file that was not a lock had its lines "
"applied as pip options. The error now names the pip version and suggests "
"``pipx upgrade-shared`` (:pr:`2289`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:254
msgid ""
"Refuse a URL spec whose installed ``METADATA`` names a different project "
"than its ``.dist-info`` directory. A wheel could rewrite that name through "
"its data files and make ``pipx install --upgrade URL`` install it into "
"another application's environment (:pr:`2236`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:257
msgid ""
"Refuse a ``--python`` value that is not a version before ``--fetch-"
"python=missing`` or ``--fetch-python=always`` looks in the standalone "
"interpreter cache. pipx joined the raw value onto ``PIPX_HOME/py`` and "
"deleted the result as a failed earlier download, so a directory path, "
"``..``, ``.`` or a bare ``python`` removed that directory, ``PIPX_HOME`` or "
"the whole interpreter cache (:pr:`2262`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:261
msgid ""
"Refuse an empty or whitespace-only ``--index-url`` instead of silently "
"installing from the default index (:pr:`2217`) by :user:`Svastikkka`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:263
msgid ""
"Refuse an empty or whitespace-only index option inside ``--pip-args`` (``--"
"index-url``, ``-i``, ``--extra-index-url``, ``--default-index``, ``--"
"index``), and under the uv backend an empty index recorded by an earlier "
"install, instead of letting uv install from the default index (:pr:`2253`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:266
msgid ""
"Refuse an environment name that is empty or a path instead of acting outside "
"``$PIPX_HOME/venvs``. ``pipx uninstall \"\"``, for example from an unset "
"shell variable, used to remove every environment and exit 0, and an "
"``install-all`` snapshot, manifest tool name or reported package name "
"holding a path built the environment at that path. pipx now stops with "
"``Invalid environment name`` (:pr:`2331`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:270
msgid ""
"Refuse to overwrite ``/etc/profile.d/pipx.sh`` or ``/etc/paths.d/pipx`` in "
"``pipx ensurepath --global`` when the file holds content pipx did not write, "
"such as an administrator's ``PIPX_GLOBAL_HOME`` or ``PIP_INDEX_URL`` "
"exports. pipx used to replace the whole file with its ``PATH`` entry and "
"report success. It now leaves the file and its mode alone and exits with an "
"error that names ``--force``, which still replaces the file. pipx replaces a "
"file that holds only an earlier pipx entry, as before (:pr:`2315`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:275
msgid ""
"Refuse to run ``pipx manifest lock`` when a tool's ``lock`` path resolves "
"outside the manifest directory, instead of replacing a ``pylock.toml`` "
"elsewhere on disk and discarding its previous contents. ``pipx manifest "
"sync`` still reads such locks (:pr:`2223`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:278
msgid ""
"Refuse to run pip or uv in an environment whose ``pyvenv.cfg`` is gone, and "
"suggest ``pipx reinstall``. Without that file the environment's ``python`` "
"link starts the interpreter it was created from, so a ``pipx upgrade`` after "
"a wheel had shipped and then dropped ``pyvenv.cfg`` installed the package "
"into that interpreter's prefix and reported success (:pr:`2326`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:282
msgid ""
"Reject ``--global``, ``--skip-maintenance``, ``--verbose`` and ``--quiet`` "
"placed between ``manifest``, ``interpreter`` or ``cache`` and their "
"subcommand, as in ``pipx manifest --global sync``. pipx accepted the option "
"there and then dropped it, so ``pipx manifest --global sync --prune`` synced "
"and pruned the per-user store with exit 0. Put the option after the "
"subcommand, as in ``pipx manifest sync --global`` (:pr:`2320`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:286
msgid ""
"Report an environment whose ``pipx_metadata.json`` the current user cannot "
"read as unreadable in ``pipx list``, instead of as missing metadata from a "
"pipx older than 0.15 that needs reinstalling. A non-root user sees this for "
"every environment of ``pipx list --global``, because pipx keeps the file "
"owner-only: it can hold index credentials. ``pipx list`` still lists the "
"environments the user can read (:pr:`2323`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:290
msgid ""
"Resolve every relative path given to a pip option, such as ``--cert "
"ca.pem``, ``-r requirements.txt``, ``--log`` or ``--cache-dir``, against the "
"directory pipx was started in, also when the option is clustered or "
"abbreviated, as in ``-qr requirements.txt`` or ``--find-l wheels``. The "
"shared pip refresh runs inside the shared libraries directory, so ``pipx "
"upgrade-shared --pip-args='--cert=ca.pem'`` failed with ``invalid path: "
"ca.pem``; installs, upgrades and ``pipx run`` now also resolve these values "
"against the starting directory (:pr:`2351`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:295
msgid ""
"Restore every earlier lock when ``pipx manifest lock`` fails because a "
"directory sits at a later tool's lock path. pipx used to stop rolling back "
"at that directory, keep the new locks of the tools before it, and delete "
"their previous versions (:pr:`2260`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:298
msgid ""
"Restore the existing environment when ``pipx install --force`` or ``pipx "
"install-all --force`` rebuilds it on another interpreter because of the "
"package's ``Requires-Python`` and the rebuild fails. pipx used to delete the "
"environment first and leave behind an empty one without its app, injected "
"packages, or ``pipx_metadata.json``, while it reported it had kept the "
"environment. It now moves the environment to its trash before the rebuild "
"and moves it back on failure (:pr:`2229`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:303
msgid ""
"Stop ``pipx ensurepath --global --force`` from crashing with "
"``UnicodeDecodeError`` when ``/etc/profile.d/pipx.sh`` or ``/etc/paths.d/"
"pipx`` holds bytes that are not UTF-8. ``--force`` now replaces the file "
"without reading it, and without ``--force`` such a file gets the same error "
"that names ``--force`` as any other file pipx did not write (:pr:`2355`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:307
msgid ""
"Stop ``pipx interpreter upgrade`` from moving an environment to another "
"Python found on ``PATH`` when the newest release of its package has a "
"``Requires-Python`` that rules out the new standalone build. The command "
"reported the patch upgrade as done while the environment now ran on, for "
"example, ``/usr/bin/python3.11``. It now fails, restores the environment on "
"its standalone build, and exits 1 (:pr:`2301`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:311
msgid ""
"Stop ``pipx upgrade-all`` from moving an app, manual page, or completion "
"that two environments expose to the other environment while the installer of "
"its owner is replacing the linked file. pipx treated any link whose target "
"was missing as left over and replaced it without ``--force``; a missing "
"target inside another environment that still exists now counts as a "
"collision (:pr:`2303`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:315
msgid ""
"Stop a self-managed pipx (``pipx install pipx``) started through its own "
"environment's script from taking that environment's ``bin`` directory for "
"``PIPX_BIN_DIR`` when the path to the script holds ``..`` or a symlinked "
"directory, such as ``../share/pipx/venvs/pipx/bin/pipx`` from ``~/.local/"
"bin``. Such a command linked the apps it installed into pipx's own "
"environment, off ``PATH`` and onto pipx's own import path. pipx now "
"recognizes the exposed link by real locations, which also works when you "
"reach the pipx home through a symlink (:pr:`2309`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:321
msgid ""
"Stop pipx from importing modules out of the directory of its own launcher "
"script, or out of the working directory under ``python -m pipx``, once "
"``pipx.__main__`` starts. After ``pip install --user pipx`` that directory "
"is ``~/.local/bin``, where pipx links apps, so pipx imported a ``json.py`` "
"or ``shlex.py`` script a package shipped there in place of the standard "
"library module, and an exposed ``json.py`` broke every later pipx command, "
"``pipx uninstall`` included. For modules pip's launcher imports before that "
"point, such as ``re`` and ``enum``, pipx refuses to expose apps named after "
"standard library modules. Programs that import ``pipx.__main__`` no longer "
"see their script directory on ``sys.path`` either (:pr:`2316`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:328
msgid ""
"Stop recording pip options that name a one-shot input or an output location, "
"such as ``-r requirements.txt``, ``--log``, ``--report``, ``--cache-dir`` or "
"``--target``: they apply to the command they were given on, and a later "
"``pipx upgrade`` or ``pipx reinstall`` no longer reads or writes those "
"paths. pipx reads pip arguments as pip does, so a clustered short option "
"such as ``-qr requirements.txt`` or an abbreviation such as ``--log-f "
"pip.log`` counts too. On POSIX, ``pipx upgrade``, ``pipx reinstall`` and the "
"other commands that replay recorded arguments stop with an error, before the "
"installer runs and without changing the record, when a recorded ``--find-"
"links``, ``--constraint``, ``--build-constraint``, ``--cert``, ``--client-"
"cert``, or ``file://`` or local-path index URL points at a path another "
"account could change. Pass the options again with ``--pip-args`` to use them "
"for that run (:pr:`2359`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:337
msgid ""
"Stop two pipx commands that fetch the same standalone Python at once from "
"leaving an interpreter with part of its standard library missing in "
"``PIPX_HOME/py``. Both staged the build in one fixed directory and each "
"deleted the other's half-copied tree as a leftover; pipx now holds a per-"
"version lock while it fetches, so the second command waits and reuses the "
"first one's build. ``pipx interpreter list``, ``prune`` and ``upgrade`` also "
"skip the staging and backup directories of a fetch in progress instead of "
"treating them as interpreters. An interpreter that an earlier fetch already "
"left incomplete still needs deleting by hand (:pr:`2293`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:343
msgid ""
"The pip backend now removes ``pip.conf`` (``pip.ini`` on Windows) from the "
"root of an environment before it starts pip there. A wheel could ship that "
"file as a data file, and pip read it as its site configuration, so a "
"``target`` or index in it made a later ``pipx upgrade`` or ``pipx inject`` "
"install outside the environment or from another index (:pr:`2264`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:347
msgid ""
"Under the uv backend, ``--index-url`` (``-i``) now reaches uv as ``--default-"
"index``. uv let ``UV_DEFAULT_INDEX`` or a default ``[[index]]`` entry "
"override a command-line ``--index-url``, so ``pipx run``, ``install``, "
"``upgrade`` and ``outdated`` used the default index instead of the one named "
"on the command line (:pr:`2247`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:350
msgid ""
"Under the uv backend, ``pipx run script.py`` now keeps the script's "
"environment in pipx's run cache, keyed to the script's path, the "
"interpreter, ``--pip-args`` and the cooldown. uv kept one environment per "
"script path and reused it while it satisfied the script, so a changed ``--"
"index-url``, ``--pip-args`` or ``--cooldown``, or ``--refresh``, still ran "
"what an earlier run installed. ``pipx cache purge`` and the 14-day expiry "
"now cover these environments (:pr:`2274`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:355
msgid ""
"Under the uv backend, ``pipx run`` now puts ``--`` before the app name it "
"hands to ``uv tool run``. An app word that started with a single dash, such "
"as ``pipx run -- -ihttp://host/simple demodep``, was read by uv as one of "
"its own options, and uv installed and ran the next word as the package "
"(:pr:`2299`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:358
msgid ""
"Under the uv backend, ``pipx upgrade``, ``upgrade-all`` and ``install --"
"upgrade`` now pass uv ``--upgrade-package NAME`` instead of ``--upgrade``, "
"so they upgrade only the named package and leave its dependencies alone "
"unless the new release needs others, as pip's default ``only-if-needed`` "
"strategy does. Before, uv upgraded every dependency, replacing packages "
"injected with ``pipx inject --force`` and pinned with ``pipx pin --injected-"
"only`` (:pr:`2248`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:363
msgid ""
"When ``pipx install`` or ``pipx run --spec`` under the pip backend has to "
"install a URL, VCS or sdist spec to learn its name, the shared pip it "
"installs along the way now comes from the command's ``--index-url`` and ``--"
"pip-args`` instead of pip's default index (:pr:`2275`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:366
msgid ""
"When an environment holds two ``.dist-info`` records with the same name, "
"pipx now reads the first one on ``sys.path``, the one the environment's "
"interpreter uses. Since 1.15.1 it read the last one, so ``--system-site-"
"packages`` with a different version of the package in the base interpreter "
"reported that version and exposed its commands (:pr:`2258`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:370
msgid ""
"``pipx install --preinstall`` and ``pipx run --with`` now refuse a value "
"that starts with ``-``. Written as ``--with=--find-links=DIR`` or ``--"
"preinstall=-rFILE``, such a value reached pip or ``uv pip install`` as an "
"installer option and changed where packages came from, instead of failing "
"like the main package spec does. Pass installer options with ``--pip-args`` "
"(:pr:`2307`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:374
msgid ""
"``pipx install-all --backend uv`` now translates index options that a pip "
"recording spells as an abbreviation pip accepts, such as ``--index-u URL``, "
"instead of dropping them and installing from the default index. A recorded "
"pip ``--index URL`` now becomes uv ``--default-index URL``, matching how pip "
"read it (:pr:`2232`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:377
msgid ""
"``pipx install`` with several packages no longer builds every environment on "
"the Python it picked for one package whose ``Requires-Python`` rules out the "
"default interpreter; the other packages keep the default Python (:pr:`2222`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:380
msgid ""
"``pipx list --outdated`` and ``pipx upgrade-all`` now check uv environments "
"against the index recorded with uv's option names (``--default-index``, ``--"
"index``, ``--allow-insecure-host``, ``--index-strategy``, ``--keyring-"
"provider``) instead of uv's default index (:pr:`2220`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:383
msgid ""
"``pipx reinstall``, ``pipx reinstall-all`` and ``pipx repair`` now refuse an "
"environment whose ``pipx_metadata.json`` is unreadable or was lost to a "
"killed install, instead of rebuilding it from the default index under the "
"directory name. ``pipx install`` marks the environment unfinished until it "
"writes the record, and ``pipx uninstall`` moves the environment to its trash "
"before deleting it, so a killed uninstall no longer leaves a venv without "
"its record (:pr:`2234`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:388
msgid ""
"``pipx run --with`` now installs the ``--with`` packages in the same "
"installer call as the app. pipx skipped a ``--with`` naming a package the "
"app already depends on, such as ``--with 'dep==1.0'``, as already installed, "
"so the app ran with the newest release on the pip backend. A ``--with`` "
"naming the app with an extra no longer links the cached environment's "
"commands into ``PIPX_BIN_DIR`` (:pr:`2266`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:392
msgid ""
"``pipx run script.py`` now expires its cache entry when creating the "
"environment fails or is interrupted, not only when installing the script's "
"dependencies does. A Ctrl-C during ``python -m venv`` left an empty cache "
"directory, and every later run of the script reused it and failed with "
"``FileNotFoundError`` until the entry expired (:pr:`2294`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:396
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` and ``pipx install`` now fail when a script download ends "
"before its ``Content-Length``. Before, pipx ran or installed the part that "
"arrived and could exit 0 (:pr:`2251`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:398
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` and ``pipx install`` now refuse an ``http`` or ``https`` script "
"URL with credentials, naming it with the password masked. Before, a URL such "
"as ``https://user:password@host/tool.py`` failed with an error that printed "
"the password in clear text and wrote it to the log. ``pipx install`` also "
"reports a malformed script URL as an error instead of a traceback "
"(:pr:`2249`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:402
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` no longer keys its cache on the ``PIP_*`` and ``UV_*`` "
"variables that cannot change what the installer resolves or installs: "
"timeouts, retries, parallelism, verbosity, progress and color output, cache "
"directories, and the ``UV_RUN_RECURSION_DEPTH`` that ``uv run`` sets for its "
"children. Setting one of them rebuilt the environment for an unchanged "
"command. Every other variable with those prefixes stays in the key, whatever "
"its case or ``-``/``_`` spelling, since pip reads ``PIP_index_url`` the same "
"as ``PIP_INDEX_URL`` (:pr:`2353`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:407
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` now includes the installer's environment variables (``PIP_*``, "
"or ``UV_*`` under the uv backend) in its cache key. A run after changing "
"``PIP_INDEX_URL``, ``PIP_FIND_LINKS`` or ``UV_INDEX_URL`` reused the "
"environment built from the previous index for up to 14 days (:pr:`2282`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:410
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` now keys its cache on the absolute path of a local ``--spec``, "
"``--with`` or ``--find-links`` value. The same relative path typed in two "
"directories, such as ``--spec ./dist/tool-1.0-py3-none-any.whl``, shared one "
"environment, so the second directory ran the first directory's build by "
"Bernát Gábor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:413
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` now names the script URL, with credentials masked, when a "
"download fails, as ``pipx install`` already did. ``pipx install`` of a "
"script URL whose body does not decode in its declared charset, or declares "
"an unknown one, now reports an error instead of a traceback, as ``pipx run`` "
"already did (:pr:`2255`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:416
msgid ""
"``pipx runpip <venv> install`` now records a relative ``--find-links`` (``-"
"f``) path resolved against the directory you ran it from. Before, a later "
"``pipx upgrade`` or ``pipx reinstall`` read it against the environment's "
"directory, failed with ``Failed to read --find-links directory`` or ``No "
"matching distribution found``, and rolled back (:pr:`2349`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:420
msgid ""
"``pipx runpip`` starts pip or uv in your working directory again instead of "
"the environment's root, so relative paths such as ``-r requirements.txt``, "
"``-c constraints.txt`` or ``./dist/app.whl`` name your files. Since 1.12.0 "
"the installer looked them up in the environment, where they were missing or "
"named a data file an installed wheel had put there (:pr:`2318`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:424
msgid ""
"``pipx uninject`` no longer removes apps, man pages and completions that the "
"main package or another injected package of the environment still exposes, "
"such as a command of a dependency both packages share under ``--include-"
"deps`` (:pr:`2296`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:427
msgid ""
"``pipx uninject`` now ignores installed distributions whose metadata "
"``Name`` is not a valid project name when it looks for orphaned dependencies "
"to remove. A name such as ``-t/some/dir`` or ``-rFILE`` reached ``uv pip "
"uninstall`` or ``pip uninstall`` as an option, and with uv could delete "
"packages from a directory outside pipx (:pr:`2306`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:431
msgid ""
"pipx no longer crashes on Python 3.11 and 3.12 when a package's ``installed-"
"files.txt`` lists a looping symlink, and skips that entry instead "
"(:pr:`2336`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:433
msgid ""
"pipx no longer exposes an app whose name is a standard library module or "
"``pipx`` plus an import suffix, such as ``enum.py``, ``re.pyc`` or "
"``pipx.py``, or a directory named after one, and warns instead. Python "
"searches the directory of the script it starts first, so in ``~/.local/bin`` "
"such an app replaced the module for pip's ``pipx`` launcher, which imports "
"``re`` and then ``pipx`` before pipx can drop that directory from "
"``sys.path``, and for every other Python script installed there (:pr:`2342`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:438
msgid ""
"pipx no longer reads ``installed-files.txt`` from a distribution that has a "
"``RECORD``, matching ``importlib.metadata``. A dependency, or a package "
"injected without ``--include-apps``, could ship that file into the main "
"package's ``.dist-info`` and get its own apps, man pages and completions "
"exposed without ``--include-deps`` (:pr:`2277`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:442
msgid ""
"pipx now adds ``-E`` to an app script's shebang by writing a new file and "
"renaming it over the script, instead of writing into the existing file. With "
"the uv backend the script can be a hard link or symlink into uv's cache, so "
"the in-place write also changed the cache entry and the same script in every "
"other environment uv had installed that wheel into (:pr:`2285`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:446
msgid ""
"pipx now reads a package's ``entry_points.txt`` only when that package's "
"``RECORD`` lists it, or when the package has no ``RECORD``. A dependency "
"could ship that file into the ``.dist-info`` of a main package that has no "
"entry points of its own and get its apps exposed without ``--include-deps`` "
"(:pr:`2340`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

