msgid "Documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:455
msgid ""
"Document what the security policy covers: which inputs pipx trusts, and "
"which reports count as vulnerabilities (:pr:`2198`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:463
msgid ""
"A bare package name such as ``pipx install pycowsay`` now always means the "
"package on the index. A file of that name without a suffix in the working "
"directory no longer gets installed as a PEP 723 script; pass a path such as "
"``./pycowsay`` to install one. URL specs no longer pick up a script at the "
"matching relative path below the working directory either (:pr:`2243`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:467
msgid ""
"Ask the Python Launcher for Unix for a ``--python`` value only when it is an "
"``X`` or ``X.Y`` version. The launcher ran any other value, such as "
"``3.14.8`` or ``3.13t``, on the first interpreter its search found, which "
"could be a ``.venv`` in a parent of the current directory (:pr:`2242`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:470
msgid ""
"Create the self-managed bootstrap environment in the installation guide with "
"``mktemp -d`` instead of the fixed ``/tmp/bootstrap`` path, which another "
"local user could create first and plant code in that ran as the reader, and "
"as root at the ``sudo`` step (:pr:`2219`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:473
msgid ""
"Look up a command name in ``PIPX_DEFAULT_PYTHON``, such as ``python3``, on "
"``PATH`` only: pipx no longer uses a file of that name in the current "
"directory as the default interpreter. Write ``./python3`` to pick that file "
"on purpose (:pr:`2226`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:476
msgid ""
"Pass the absolute path ``PATH`` lookup found for ``--python python3.11`` on "
"to the backend instead of the bare name. uv read the bare name as a version "
"request and could pick a ``.venv`` interpreter from a parent of the current "
"directory. A file in the current directory named like the value, such as ``./"
"3.11``, no longer counts as a path either (:pr:`2240`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:480
msgid ""
"Read a package name from a local ``pyproject.toml`` or wheel only for local "
"path specs. A URL spec such as ``https://host/app.whl`` no longer takes its "
"name, and with it the target environment, from a file at the matching "
"relative path below the working directory (:pr:`2238`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:483
msgid ""
"Record relative ``--find-links`` and ``--constraint`` values passed to "
"``pipx upgrade --pip-args`` and ``pipx run`` scripts as absolute paths, "
"resolve relative values already in ``pipx_metadata.json`` against the "
"environment's directory, and run the shared pip refresh inside the shared "
"libraries directory, so a later ``pipx upgrade`` or ``pipx reinstall`` no "
"longer reads wheels from whatever directory you start it in (:pr:`2233`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:487
msgid ""
"Record the index options of a ``pipx runpip <venv> install`` that replaces "
"the main package, so a later ``pipx upgrade`` or ``pipx reinstall`` asks the "
"same index instead of resolving the bare name on the default one "
"(:pr:`2231`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:490
msgid ""
"Start scripts read from a URL or a named pipe, ``pipx.run`` entry points, "
"and apps run with ``--python-args`` with ``python -P`` so a module in the "
"current directory, such as a planted ``json.py``, no longer shadows what the "
"program imports (:pr:`2221`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:493
msgid ""
"Stop ``pipx reinstall`` from replacing the main package while it replays "
"injected packages. The replay passed ``--force-reinstall``, so an injected "
"package that depends on the main package made the installer fetch the main "
"package again by name from the injected package's index and install that "
"release over the recorded source. ``pipx inject --force`` now passes ``--"
"force-reinstall`` only when the package is already injected, and under the "
"uv backend reinstalls just that package with ``--reinstall-package`` "
"(:pr:`2227`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:498
msgid ""
"Stop ``pipx run`` from retrying a failed uv install with pip. A venv "
"directory without ``pipx_metadata.json`` no longer counts as recorded with "
"the pip backend, so it resolves its backend like a new venv, and a ``pipx "
"run`` whose install fails now expires its cache entry so the next run "
"rebuilds it. pip ignores ``UV_INDEX_URL``, so the retry fetched the package "
"from pip's default index instead of the private one (:pr:`2235`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:502
msgid ""
"The uv backend no longer applies a ``uv.toml`` or ``pyproject.toml`` found "
"in the directory uv runs in, the script's directory, or their parents, such "
"as one another local account wrote to a shared ``/tmp``. pipx now points "
"uv's project-config search at ``PIPX_HOME`` through ``UV_PROJECT``, and "
"through ``--project`` for ``uv run --script``. Your user and system "
"``uv.toml`` and ``UV_CONFIG_FILE`` still apply. Keep ``PIPX_HOME`` out of "
"directories other accounts can write (:pr:`2246`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:507
msgid ""
"When ``pipx install --force`` or ``pipx manifest sync`` rebuilds an existing "
"environment, either on another Python because the release's ``Requires-"
"Python`` rules out the current one or to apply a lock file, keep the backend "
"recorded for that environment. The rebuild used to pick the backend as for a "
"new environment, so a pip-backed environment could move to uv and install "
"from uv's default index instead of the one set in ``PIP_INDEX_URL`` or "
"``pip.conf`` (:pr:`2237`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:512
msgid ""
"``pipx inject ENV 'APP[extra]'`` now adds the extra to the main package's "
"recorded source instead of replacing it with the bare name ``APP[extra]``. "
"An app installed from a wheel, a directory or a URL no longer turns into the "
"index's project of the same name on the next ``pipx upgrade`` or ``pipx "
"reinstall``. Extras accumulate with the ones already recorded, and a main-"
"package spec that changes the version, path or URL needs ``--force`` "
"(:pr:`2250`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:517
msgid ""
"``pipx manifest sync`` now keeps the installer and venv options recorded for "
"an environment that already exists, such as ``--index-url``. It used to "
"reinstall the tool from the default index and erase the recorded options "
"(:pr:`2224`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:520
msgid ""
"pipx now creates its log directory readable by its owner only (``0700``), "
"tightens an existing one, and writes ``cmd_*.log`` and ``cmd_*_{pip,uv}"
"_errors.log`` as ``0600``. The logs record the full command line, including "
"the arguments ``pipx run`` and ``pipx exec`` pass to the application, and in "
"a ``--global`` store under ``/opt/pipx/logs`` any local account could read "
"them (:pr:`2230`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:528
msgid "`1.18.7 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.18.7>`_ - 2026-10-28"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:535
msgid ""
"Require pip 26.2.2 or later in the shared libraries, and replace an older "
"shared pip on the next pipx command instead of waiting for the 30-day "
"refresh. Older pip releases bundle a certifi that still trusts the "
"compromised eMudhra/emSign root CA (:pr:`2197`) by :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:542
msgid "`1.18.6 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.18.6>`_ - 2026-10-28"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:549
msgid ""
"Keep the extras on a local archive named without ``./``, so ``pipx install "
"\"tool-1.0-py3-none-any.whl[cow]\"`` installs the ``cow`` extra like ``./"
"tool-1.0-py3-none-any.whl[cow]`` does. A version specifier, URL or "
"environment marker after such a name now fails with an error instead of "
"being silently dropped (:pr:`2174`) by :user:`Cyber-Marty` "
"and :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:553
msgid ""
"Keep the recorded source of a local wheel when ``pipx runpip <venv> "
"install`` passes an option value that names the package, such as ``--only-"
"binary <name>``, ``--no-binary <name>``, or uv's ``--upgrade-package "
"<name>`` (:pr:`2166`) by :user:`dailyun` and :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:556
msgid ""
"Read the full inline script metadata block when a TOML multiline string in "
"it contains a ``# ///`` line, instead of failing with ``Unterminated "
"string``. As the inline script metadata specification requires, the block "
"now ends at the last ``# ///`` line of its comment run (:pr:`2172`) "
"by :user:`zurrll` and :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:559
msgid ""
"Retain commands enabled by additional dependency extras with ``--include-"
"deps`` (:pr:`2185`) by :user:`JackyHsu-X` and :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:561
msgid ""
"``pipx install pkg-1.0.tar.xz`` and other bare filenames ending in an "
"archive extension pip accepts (``.tar.bz2``, ``.tgz``, ``.tar`` and the "
"rest, in any letter case) now install the local file instead of looking up a "
"mangled project name on PyPI (:pr:`2177`) by :user:`ShahabAhmed01` "
"and :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:564
msgid ""
"``pipx upgrade-all --pip-args=--index-url``, or any other index option given "
"without a value, now fails with an error naming the option instead of a "
"``StopIteration`` traceback, and ``--output json`` reports it in the usual "
"error envelope (:pr:`2182`) by :user:`jdotc1` and :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:573
msgid ""
"Fix the dead PythonBytes episode link on the docs home page (:pr:`2170`) "
"by :user:`qodelicious` and :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:575
msgid ""
"Use a current black commit in the install-from-commit example (:pr:`2181`) "
"by :user:`dcadolph` and :user:`gaborbernat`."
msgstr ""

