msgid "`1.17.12 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.12>`_ - 2026-10-07"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:766
msgid ""
"Stop `pipx reinstall` from printing a traceback when the reinstall fails for "
"an expected reason. (:pr:`2070`) by :user:`ParamTanna`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:768
msgid ""
"Stop `pipx install` printing `WARNING: Skipping setuptools as it is not "
"installed.` when the shared libraries are created on Python 3.12+, where "
"setuptools is already absent. (:pr:`2071`) by :user:`officialpm` "
"and :user:`gaborbernat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:771
msgid ""
"Stop an injected package in a suffixed environment from being renamed every "
"time its record is rewritten: `pipx upgrade`, `pipx pin` and `pipx "
"reinstall` no longer append the environment suffix again, so the package "
"keeps its name in `pipx list --include-injected` and stays addressable by "
"`pipx uninject`. (:pr:`2072`) by :user:`feiiiiii5` and :user:`gaborbernat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:781
msgid "Update the pipx logo author credit. (:issue:`2073`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:786
msgid "`1.17.11 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.11>`_ - 2026-10-03"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:793
msgid ""
"Hide the extra documentation TOC toggle on narrow screens. (:issue:`2064`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:798
msgid "`1.17.10 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.10>`_ - 2026-10-02"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:805
msgid ""
"Remove an environment that has no pipx metadata and an interpreter that no "
"longer runs, instead of crashing `pipx uninstall` and `pipx uninstall-all`. "
"(:pr:`2059`) by :user:`hemcharan710-afk` and :user:`gaborbernat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:807
msgid ""
"Derive local script command names from the filename when parent directories "
"contain `#`. A script installed by an earlier release under its directory's "
"name no longer upgrades; uninstall it and install it again. (:issue:`2060`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:809
msgid ""
"Install a local PEP 723 script from its file when the path reads as a PyPI "
"name (`pipx install bare.py`), contains `[`, or starts with a quoted `~`, "
"and stop the upgrade hint from suggesting a PyPI reinstall for a script. "
"(:pr:`2062`) by :user:`gaborbernat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:816
msgid "`1.17.9 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.9>`_ - 2026-10-01"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:823
msgid ""
"Stop adding ` -E` to an app script's shebang when the longer line would "
"exceed the kernel's limit, which made the script fail on macOS with `Exec "
"format error`. (:pr:`2058`) by :user:`feiiiiii5`, :user:`OpenCode` "
"and :user:`gaborbernat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:830
msgid "`1.17.8 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.8>`_ - 2026-09-29"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:837
msgid ""
"Remove leftover shell completion scripts when running `pipx uninject`. "
"(:issue:`2055`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:842
msgid "`1.17.7 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.7>`_ - 2026-09-28"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:849
msgid ""
"Prevent `pipx run` from sharing cached environments across different "
"requirement lists or argument boundaries. This changes cache keys; run `pipx "
"cache purge` to remove old entries. (:pr:`2053`) by :user:`januththedev` "
"and :user:`gaborbernat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:856
msgid "`1.17.6 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.6>`_ - 2026-09-22"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:863
msgid ""
"Record each tool's dependency group as its lock's default so `pipx manifest "
"sync` installs what `pipx manifest lock` wrote. Run `pipx manifest lock` "
"again to fix existing locks. (:issue:`2049`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:871
msgid ""
"Fix the argument order in the combined inject command example. (:pr:`2044`) "
"by :user:`agammann`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:872
msgid ""
"Use direct URL requirements for the Git install example with extras. "
"(:issue:`2045`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:877
msgid "`1.17.5 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.5>`_ - 2026-09-20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:884
msgid ""
"Report failed environments when running `pipx reinstall-all`. (:issue:`2042`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:889
msgid "`1.17.4 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.4>`_ - 2026-09-18"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:896
msgid ""
"`pipx upgrade` of a package installed from a local path, wheel, or VCS URL "
"no longer reports \"already at latest version\". It now says the package is "
"unchanged because it is installed from a local source and that no package "
"index was checked, and suggests reinstalling by package name to track index "
"releases. (:issue:`2040`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:903
msgid "`1.17.3 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.3>`_ - 2026-09-16"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:910
msgid ""
"Report a clear error when PIPX_MAX_LOGS is not a non-negative integer, "
"instead of crashing on every pipx command. Empty or whitespace-only values "
"fall back to the default everywhere, including log setup. (:pr:`2029`) "
"by :user:`hktitof`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:913
msgid ""
"Split `--pip-args` the way a shell would, so a quoted path with spaces such "
"as `--find-links '/tmp/foo bar'` reaches pip intact instead of failing to "
"parse. On Windows pipx now drops the quotes around each argument and keeps "
"backslashes as path separators. (:pr:`2033`) by :user:`r3wretrhy`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:916
msgid ""
"Stop `pipx runpip` from printing uv DEBUG logs on the uv backend. "
"(:pr:`2035`) by :user:`anandghegde`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:923
msgid ""
"List every `--pip-args` flag the uv backend translates instead of only four. "
"(:pr:`2037`) by :user:`hxperl` and :user:`claude`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:929
msgid "`1.17.2 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.2>`_ - 2026-09-01"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:936
msgid ""
"Fix `KeyError` stderr noise when installing packages in Python3.15. "
"(:pr:`2026`) by :user:`Cycloctane`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:941
msgid "`1.17.1 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.1>`_ - 2026-08-30"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:948
msgid ""
"`pipx environment` now reports `PIPX_MAX_LOGS`, and `pipx environment --"
"value PIPX_MAX_LOGS` no longer exits with `invalid choice`. (:pr:`2024`) "
"by :user:`dylanpulver` and :user:`gaborbernat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:954
msgid "`1.17.0 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.17.0>`_ - 2026-08-29"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:961
msgid ""
"Add `PIPX_COOLDOWN`, a default for `--cooldown` on `install`, `install-all`, "
"`inject`, `upgrade`, `upgrade-all` and `run`, so one release-age policy "
"covers every command. An explicit `--cooldown` still wins, `--cooldown 0` "
"opts a single command out, and a locked install ignores the variable rather "
"than failing. (:issue:`2014`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:970
msgid ""
"Require `packaging>=26`. Earlier releases serialize a direct reference as "
"`name@ url` rather than PEP 508's `name @ url`, so the specifier pipx "
"recorded in `pipx_metadata.json` and passed to the backend depended on which "
"`packaging` happened to be installed. (:issue:`2015`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:977
msgid "`1.16.8 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.8>`_ - 2026-08-25"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:984
msgid ""
"`pipx run --spec <spec> <app>` on the uv backend builds a pipx-managed venv "
"when `<app>` differs from the spec's normalized distribution name, or when "
"the spec carries no name at all, so pipx honors the package's `[pipx.run]` "
"entry point. An `<app>` that matches the name still runs through `uv tool "
"run`, which sees console scripts only. (:issue:`2004`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:994
msgid ""
"The CLI reference in the documentation now shows `pipx run` instead of "
"`sphinx-build run`. (:issue:`2005`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:999
msgid "`1.16.7 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.7>`_ - 2026-08-13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1006
msgid ""
"Fix pipx not being able to discover packages in separated platlib "
"directories. (:pr:`1999`) by :user:`Cycloctane` and :user:`gaborbernat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1008
msgid ""
"Retry transient failures when fetching the python-build-standalone release "
"index and downloading interpreter archives, resuming an interrupted archive "
"download from the bytes already received instead of starting over. "
"(:pr:`2001`) by :user:`gaborbernat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1017
msgid ""
"Correct the documented Windows default for `PIPX_HOME`, which resolves to "
"`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\pipx\\pipx` rather than `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\pipx`. "
"(:pr:`2002`) by :user:`aroh3006`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1023
msgid "`1.16.6 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.6>`_ - 2026-08-04"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1030
msgid ""
"Stop appending a second `.exe` on Windows to the app name `pipx run` infers. "
"(:issue:`1189`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1031
msgid ""
"Run the console script a package declares when `pipx run` infers the app "
"name from a VCS URL, a local path, or a name it normalized, instead of "
"passing a guess to `uv tool run`. Reusing that venv no longer reinstalls the "
"package on every run. (:issue:`1994`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1038
msgid "`1.16.5 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.5>`_ - 2026-07-29"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1045
msgid ""
"Honor the version specifier when `pipx upgrade --install` installs a missing "
"package. (:issue:`1987`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1050
msgid "`1.16.4 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.4>`_ - 2026-07-29"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1057
msgid ""
"Bundle `colorama` and `tomli` in the zipapp so the single `pipx.pyz` works "
"on Windows and on Python 3.10. (:issue:`1978`, :issue:`1984`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1059
msgid ""
"Fix the Release Notes link published in package metadata. (:issue:`1980`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1060
msgid ""
"`PIPX_MAX_LOGS=0` now prunes the log files instead of keeping all of them. "
"(:pr:`1988`) by :user:`marko1olo`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1067
msgid ""
"Fix the documentation links that 404 after the Sphinx move, including the "
"PyPI Release Notes link. (:issue:`1980`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1072
msgid "`1.16.3 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.3>`_ - 2026-07-26"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1079
msgid ""
"Allow read-only global list commands when venv lock files are inaccessible. "
"(:issue:`1974`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1086
msgid ""
"Direct Linux users to PEP 668-compatible installation methods. "
"(:issue:`1976`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1091
msgid "`1.16.2 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.2>`_ - 2026-07-21"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1098
msgid ""
"Stop venv inspection from crashing on Python 3.15 when a `dist-info` "
"directory has no `Name` metadata field. `importlib.metadata` now raises "
"`KeyError` for missing metadata keys instead of returning `None`; such "
"distributions are skipped again, as on earlier Python versions. (:pr:`1971`) "
"by :user:`gaborbernat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1105
msgid "`1.16.1 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.1>`_ - 2026-07-20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1112
msgid ""
"Stop `install` and `list` from crashing when the pipx bin directory contains "
"an executable pipx did not create. Scanning for launcher ownership decoded "
"arbitrary binary content as an interpreter path, which raised "
"`UnicodeDecodeError` on Windows, or `ValueError` for a path holding a NUL "
"byte. Such a file is now treated as not owned by the venv. (:issue:`1965`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1120
msgid "`1.16.0 <https://github.com/pypa/pipx/tree/1.16.0>`_ - 2026-07-15"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1127
msgid "Add `pipx list --outdated` and JSON output. (:issue:`149`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1128
msgid ""
"Honour the `requires-python` a package declares. When the default "
"interpreter fails it, pipx looks for one on the system that satisfies it and "
"builds the environment there, so `pipx install mytool` no longer needs the "
"user to work out the right `--python`. Pass `--fetch-python=missing` to let "
"pipx download a matching interpreter when the system carries none, and name "
"`--python` yourself to keep the last word. (:issue:`387`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1132
msgid "Normalize inferred `pipx run` package names. (:issue:`618`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1133
msgid "Allow `pipx list` to select installed packages by name. (:issue:`640`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1134
msgid "Add `--output` to structured commands. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1135
msgid ""
"Freeze the structured result envelope at `pipx_result_version` 1. Every `--"
"output json` document now carries the command as a list of CLI tokens, a "
"`status` of `success`, `partial`, or `error`, the process `exit_code`, the "
"command `data`, and a top-level `errors` list whose entries each have a "
"stable `code` and `message` alongside the `environment` and `package` they "
"concern. A failure that stops a command before it builds a result renders "
"the same envelope. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1140
msgid "Add quiet and JSON output for package maintenance. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1141
msgid ""
"Give `pipx reinstall` and `pipx reinstall-all` the structured output the "
"other commands carry. They printed straight to the terminal, so `--quiet` "
"left `uninstalled NAME!` behind and no `--output json` existed to read the "
"result from a script. Both now report through the shared renderer. "
"(:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1144
msgid ""
"Give `pipx cache`, `pipx interpreter`, `pipx upgrade-shared`, `pipx manifest "
"lock` and `pipx manifest sync` the structured output the other commands "
"carry, so `--quiet` silences them and `--output json` hands a script the "
"result. The `cache` and `interpreter` subcommands take `--quiet` and `--"
"verbose` for the first time, since the shared options had passed them by. "
"`pipx ensurepath` goes on printing its guidance, because its job is to tell "
"a person what to add to a shell profile. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1149
msgid ""
"Add `--output json` to `pipx inject` and `pipx uninject`. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1150
msgid "Infer the app name when running packages from VCS URLs. (:issue:`854`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1151
msgid "Stream installer output during verbose installs. (:issue:`1069`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1152
msgid ""
"Draw the download progress bar of `pip` and `uv` during a plain `pipx "
"install`, in place of the pipx spinner. pipx hands the installer a pseudo-"
"terminal, which is the only way `uv` reports progress, and asks `uv` for its "
"default output rather than the quiet one. A redirected stream keeps the "
"previous behaviour. (:issue:`1069`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1155
msgid "Allow commands to skip shared-library maintenance. (:issue:`1278`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1156
msgid "Install PEP 723 scripts as persistent applications. (:issue:`1388`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1157
msgid ""
"Point library install errors to `inject` and `--preinstall`. (:issue:`1411`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1158
msgid ""
"Add commands to diagnose and repair broken environment interpreters. "
"(:issue:`1442`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1159
msgid ""
"Add explicit tool manifests with separate PEP 751 locks. (:issue:`1506`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1160
msgid ""
"Add `pipx install --upgrade` to reconcile apps with package specs. "
"(:issue:`1572`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1161
msgid ""
"Expose the shell completion scripts a package ships, the way pipx already "
"exposes its man pages. A wheel that installs into `share/bash-completion/"
"completions`, `share/zsh/site-functions` or `share/fish/"
"vendor_completions.d` gets those files linked under `PIPX_COMPLETION_DIR`, "
"which defaults to `~/.local/share`. `bash` and `fish` read those locations "
"on their own; `zsh` needs the site-functions directory on its `fpath`. "
"Uninstalling the package takes the links away. (:issue:`1604`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1166
msgid ""
"Add `pipx reset`, which uninstalls every pipx-managed package and removes "
"the shared libraries, the caches, the standalone interpreters, the logs and "
"the trash, so pipx starts over from a fresh install. It asks before it "
"removes anything, `--yes` answers for a script, and `--dry-run` lists what "
"would go. (:issue:`1606`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1169
msgid "Add Python interpreter arguments to `pipx run`. (:issue:`1613`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1170
msgid ""
"Add commands to hide and restore resources exposed from an environment. "
"(:issue:`1645`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1171
msgid "Install the generated pipx manual page from wheels. (:issue:`1657`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1172
msgid "Add `pipx cache` and `pipx run --refresh`. (:issue:`1681`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1173
msgid "Add `--include-apps-from` for selected dependencies. (:issue:`1725`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1174
msgid ""
"Add `pipx exec ENVIRONMENT APPLICATION` for installed environments. "
"(:issue:`1726`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1175
msgid "Support injecting extras into a main package. (:issue:`1805`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1176
msgid "Install from PEP 751 lock files. (:issue:`1807`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1177
msgid "Add dependency cooldowns. (:issue:`1811`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1178
msgid ""
"Validate requested apps and restore prior environments on failure. "
"(:issue:`1908`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1179
msgid ""
"Default `PIPX_HOME` to the platform data directory on macOS and Windows "
"again, which restores `~/Library/Application Support/pipx` on macOS. "
"`platformdirs` reads `XDG_DATA_HOME` and `XDG_CACHE_HOME` on macOS, so "
"exporting those moves the pipx directories. A pipx home from an earlier "
"release keeps working as a fallback. (:issue:`1946`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1182
msgid ""
"Group the manifest commands under `pipx manifest`: use `pipx manifest lock` "
"and `pipx manifest sync` in place of the top-level `pipx lock` and `pipx "
"sync`. Keeping both verbs under one noun matches `pipx cache` and `pipx "
"interpreter` and leaves the top-level command list about the manifest rather "
"than two loose verbs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1185
msgid ""
"Keep `--json` only on `pipx list`, where it prints the versioned package "
"snapshot that `install-all` reads back. Every other command dropped the `--"
"json` alias in favour of `--output json`, so the snapshot format and the "
"result envelope no longer share a flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1188
msgid ""
"Name the existing-environment argument `ENVIRONMENT` across `inject`, "
"`uninject`, `expose`, `unexpose`, `pin`, `unpin`, `uninstall`, `reinstall`, "
"and `exec`, and fix the `uninject` help, which described the argument as the "
"environment to inject into rather than uninject from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1191
msgid ""
"Record the interpreter and backend in the structured `install`, `upgrade`, "
"and `upgrade-all` results, list `PIPX_GLOBAL_COMPLETION_DIR` in `pipx "
"environment`, and show the shell-completion directory in `pipx list`. "
"Completions had a global override that pipx honoured but never surfaced, and "
"the records omitted which Python and backend produced a venv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1195
msgid ""
"Rename `--include-apps-from` to `--include-resources-from` and the manifest "
"key to match. The option always exposed manual pages and shell completions "
"alongside apps, so the new name describes what it does; `--include-apps` "
"keeps its name. A venv recorded under the old key is migrated on read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1198
msgid "Support standalone Python downloads on Windows ARM64. (:issue:`1856`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1205
msgid ""
"Check a candidate interpreter's real patch version against `requires-"
"python`. pipx matched only on the minor version, so it rejected an installed "
"`3.13.7` for `>=3.13.5` and accepted `3.14.6` for `<3.14.1`. It now queries "
"each resolved interpreter and keeps the first whose full version satisfies "
"the constraint. (:issue:`387`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1208
msgid ""
"Keep existing exposed files when copy-based environments provide the same "
"resource name. (:issue:`540`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1209
msgid ""
"Recover custom paths when pipx manages its own installation on Unix. "
"(:issue:`774`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1210
msgid ""
"Keep install failures in JSON with the correct environment. (:issue:`828`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1211
msgid ""
"Show injected apps in `pipx list` on systems that copy launchers. "
"(:issue:`997`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1212
msgid ""
"Serialize shared-library maintenance across pipx processes. (:issue:`1056`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1213
msgid ""
"Wait for an installation before listing its environment. (:issue:`1056`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1214
msgid ""
"Draw the installer progress bar while the download runs. pipx reads the "
"installer output over a pipe, which hid the terminal from `pip`, so `pip` "
"held its bar back and printed a finished one once the download had ended. "
"(:issue:`1069`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1217
msgid ""
"Preserve symlinks in `PIPX_HOME` when creating environments. (:issue:`1327`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1218
msgid "Create Windows launchers for PEP 723 scripts. (:issue:`1388`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1219
msgid ""
"Preserve the terminal encoding for applications started by `pipx run`. "
"(:issue:`1423`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1220
msgid ""
"Make `ensurepath --global` update the system PATH configuration instead of "
"root's shell profiles. (:issue:`1452`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1221
msgid ""
"Refresh `pipx_metadata.json` after `pipx runpip ... install` replaces the "
"main package, so future `upgrade` and `reinstall` commands stop following a "
"stale editable source path. (:issue:`1473`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1223
msgid ""
"Accept bare local Git and Mercurial URLs such as `git+file:///path/to/"
"repository@revision`. (:issue:`1583`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1224
msgid "Recreate the shared environment when pip cannot run. (:issue:`1606`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1225
msgid ""
"Resolve local `--find-links` paths before pipx changes the working "
"directory. (:issue:`1637`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1226
msgid ""
"Keep pipx startup usable when locked files prevent trash cleanup. "
"(:issue:`1847`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.rst:1227
msgid ""
